7:- One Invitation row per Round and Person, created at open, with a 128-bit base64url token stored only as a hash (in D1 for lookup and in the DO). The token is revoked when the member is removed or the Round is cancelled.
8-- The Invitation email has:
9-  - the Pulse name;
10-  - a one-line anonymity statement;
11:  - five text-labelled rating links `https://app.surveybeat.app/a#t=<token>&v=<n>` (the **token is in the fragment**);
12-  - "Open check-in";
13-  - up to three Actions (an empty slot until slice 13);
--
19-  - skipped if the member has answered, has opted out, or close is less than 2 hours away.
20-- Reminder opt-out per Person per Pulse: RFC 8058 `List-Unsubscribe` with a POST endpoint, no redirect, and DKIM-covered headers.
21:- The "Change when I get this" page runs on the Main Worker, with the token in the POST body. It suggests the browser's time zone and never touches answers.
22-- The Lead's view lists failed Invitations with their reason and a **Resend** button.
